RULING (disclosure 1): the inversion does NOT touch the red-provenance class.
That class is about reds produced after the code they are supposed to have
preceded; these reds predate the implementation tree, name the skeleton in their
own output, and I demonstrated in §3 that the suite bites when the mechanisms
they cover are removed. No rule in this repo orders `ready` against `red` —
process.ts:312-324 (`process.tdd`) only compares source-vs-test in the last
commit, and there is no timestamp rule anywhere. Harmless sequencing slip.
The substantive issue that travels with it is §5.2, which is a different class.

